<h1>Preferences - Datums - Capture Method</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Datum Capture settings define behaviour of the software during datum capture.</p>
<p><img src="../images/preferences_datums_capture_method.gif" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p id="p2" class="sub-head">Point Capture Method group</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Capture stream of datum points means that a datum point is generated by single click (capture) and no Accept/Reject dialog appears. The behaviour is similar to Capture Static Points (<span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Performance Check Utilities &gt; Capture Static Points</b></i></span>). This increases the speed of datum points capture.</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Capture stream of points is applicable to the following capture commands:</p>
<ol type="1" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Point  uncompensated point.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">2D Point &gt; Planar  this is the method where a plane and points are captured, then the points are fitted and the resulting point is projected onto the plane.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Single point</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Every resulting datum point is fitted by one or more captured points and Accept/Reject dialog appears before the point is created. This is the default method.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a22" style="text-decoration:underline;">Workflow for point (uncompensated)</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP173846066" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/Single_Point_capture.gif" width="485px" height="371px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Workflow for 2D point (planar)</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171572278" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/Single_Surface_Point_capture.gif" width="648px" height="721px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Stream of points</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Every resulting datum point is created by one captured point and no Accept/Reject dialog appears.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Workflow for point (uncompensated)</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP173723843" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/Stream_Point_capture.gif" width="574px" height="370px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Workflow for 2D point (planar)</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP169455244" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/Stream_Surface_Point_capture.gif" width="646px" height="610px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p id="h21" class="sub-head">Base Plane Definition group</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">This option defines the behaviour of the capture wizard for entities, which need base plane, i.e.:</p>
<ol type="1" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">2D Line.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Circle.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Rectangular slot.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Round slot.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Prompt</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If there are other plane reducible entities in the scene (like plane, circle, cylinder (top/bottom base), cone (base), round slot, or rectangular slot) then a dialog displays list of all such entities with '<span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Capture 3 or more points to define a plane</i></span>' command on top. If this command is selected user should capture the base plane for the feature that will be measured. Otherwise the selected entity will be used as base plane.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Always capture</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The base plane for the feature that will be measured will always be captured regardless of the presence of other plane reducible entities.</p>
<p id="h23" class="sub-head">Datum Capture Method group</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">This option defines the behaviour of the capture wizard for entities, which have tactile and scanning capture methods. These entities are:</p>
<ol type="1" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Plane.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Sphere.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Cylinder.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Circle.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Cone.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Rectangular slot.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Round slot.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Prompt</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets the wizard to ask for capture method.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Tactile</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Wizard immediately switches to tactile capture. Enabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Scanning</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Wizard immediately switches to scanning capture.</p>
<p id="h22" class="sub-head"><span lang="EN-GB">B</span>utton</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Default</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets all settings to their default values.</p>

